# Vera Navigation (non-negotiable)

Every authenticated Vera page MUST use the unified navigation system.

## Required structure

1. **Global header** — `Header` (`VeraGlobalHeader`) with `GlobalNav` in the same position on every signed-in page
2. **Module bar** — `ModuleHeader` (`VeraModuleBar`) with `ModuleNav` when the route belongs to a module
3. **Content** — `ContentContainer` for the main region; `PageLayout` (`VeraPageLayout`) for title, filters, actions

## Shells

- Full workspace: `WorkspaceShell` / `VeraAppShell` (`/pm`, `/admin`, `/core`, …)
- Lightweight signed-in: `SignedInVeraLayout` / `VeraSignedInShell` (`/welcome`, `/hub`, `/weather`, …)

## Forbidden

- Sidebars for module switching
- Horizontal tab nav for modules or features (`AcpNav`, `HubModuleNav`, `HubNavigateDropdown`, duplicate PM links)
- Inline "← back to module" links — use module dropdown instead
- Hiding global modules based on role or context
- Module-specific header layouts

## Config

Add modules/features only in `lib/navigation/vera-nav-config.ts`.

See `docs/VERA-NAVIGATION-ARCHITECTURE.md`.
